& [Roles] are separated
  + [caller] supplies one strict plan and one completed assembly
  + [assembly] preserves carrier lineage and determines exact observation order
  + [encoder] emits only declared domain, framing, tags, and values into a hash sink
  + [hasher] derives SHA-256 over exact encoder updates
  + [validator] reruns current observation validity and output correlations
  + [result] retains plan, full assembly, encoding profile, and digest without being deserializable
  + [future_receipt_issuer] is absent and gains no authority here

& [Obligations] are expanded
  + preserve exact result profile cantor-windows-supplied-ordered-topology-inventory-digest/0.1
  + preserve exact encoding profile cantor-ordered-topology-observation-encoding/0.1
  + cap encoded plan at 4096 bytes before strict JSON decode
  + require nonzero commitment identity
  + accept only a completed assembly by value
  + require exact assembly profile, representable count, count equality, root-first shape, existing ordinal sequence, and checked total-file-byte equality
  + rerun current ValidateTopologyForm on every observation
  + begin hash input with exact ASCII encoding profile and one zero byte
  + encode entry count as u64 big endian
  + encode each observation in existing order with exact entry and field tags
  + encode every integer with fixed declared width and big endian
  + encode every enum with a closed explicit tag
  + encode optional presence, text byte length, sequence count, file identity bytes, and digest bytes exactly
  + encode every stream fact in existing validated order
  + finalize lowercase 64-hex SHA-256
  + retain the complete assembly in a private Serialize-only result
  + return no partial digest success on any failure

